special_abilities:
  - name: "Abilities Common to Lemurians"
    description: "For a Lemurian Serpent Hunter the racial abilities apply as on the race''s own page, with one change: Empathy with Animals is replaced by Empathy with Serpents & Monsters. Life Sense: 25 foot (7.6 m) radius plus 5 feet (1.5 m) per level; 20% +5% per level to locate, track or find a specific type of animal or plant, +5% underwater. Ley lines: heals and recovers P.P.E. twice as fast as a normal human on a ley line or at a stone pyramid, and swims 25% faster along one. Ultrasonic communication: 2,000 feet (610 m) underwater, 400 feet (122 m) on the surface or in the air. Likely to be accompanied by an Aquatic Lemur."
  - name: "Empathy with Serpents & Monsters"
    description: "Replaces the Lemurian Empathy with Animals. Covers serpents, sea serpents, sea monsters, snakes, large reptiles, predators and other monsters (dinosaurs count as monsters). Rapport: 80% +1% per level, +8% when the creature is an actual serpent. On a success the creature stays wary but does not attack, and if the Hunter moves slowly and without threat it lets itself be led from prey, touched, handled, examined, groomed, treated or milked of venom, and tolerates him in its lair and at its food. On a failure it growls a warning and attacks if he does not back off. Dominance (after 1D4 melee rounds of grooming and petting once rapport is made): 70% +1% per level, +10% for an actual serpent, +15% for an already tamed War Steed or domesticated animal, -20% against a sentient monster with even a low human-equivalent I.Q.; not applicable to true dragons and greater supernatural beings. Failure is the same warning, then an attack. Success makes the Hunter the creature''s equal or superior, not its master: he can play and wrestle with it, care for its young, handle it roughly, hunt beside it, keep it as an ally and ride it, and can ask it to fight beside him, but it cannot be forced to do anything. In a life and death fight or against something it fears it may refuse and leave, with a 50/50 chance that it hangs back and joins in when it sees an advantage. Penalty: with every other kind of animal, domesticated ones included, the Hunter is -20% on riding and other animal skills."
  - name: "Horsemanship: Serpent Hunter (Ride Sea Monsters & Sea Serpents)"
    description: "The Hunter''s war horse is a sea monster or sea serpent. Training covers riding and fighting saddled or bareback, dismounting and fighting on as a coordinated pair, and moving along the whole length of the mount - swinging from spines and fins, riding from the side or tail, hiding under a fin, upside down or inside its mouth. 70%/50% +3% per level, +10% on one of the Hunter''s two personal War Steeds, and +10% if the monster is intelligent and willing to carry him or is an actual serpent. Stored as the skill Horsemanship: Serpent Hunter."
  - name: "Sense Sea Serpents, Sea Monsters and Aquatic Monsters"
    description: "A knack for locating such quarry and for sensing when one is within one mile (1.6 km) or is stalking him. 50% +4% per level of experience, -20% on dry land."
  - name: "Dragon, Sea Serpent and Sea Monster Slaying"
    description: "+1 attack per melee when battling serpents, dragons and monsters. +2 to automatic dodge when battling them, and that dodge does not use up a melee attack. Double damage from behind. Critical Strike (double damage) on a natural 19 or 20 at level one, and on a natural 18-20 from level four. Critical Strike Death Blow (triple damage) on a natural 18-20 from level eight."
    progression:
      - { level: 4, text: "Critical Strike (double damage) on a natural 18-20." }
      - { level: 8, text: "Critical Strike Death Blow (triple damage) on a natural 18-20." }
  - name: "Spell Knowledge (Limited)"
    description: "Knows eleven spells, with their P.P.E. costs as the page prints them: Breathe Without Air (5), Globe of Daylight (2), Impervious to Fire (5), Lightblade (20), Magic Net (7), Magic Shield (6), Armor of Ithan (10), Sense Evil (2), Sense Magic (4), Tongues (12) and Chameleon (6). The Hunter is limited to this list and may not learn new spells. P.P.E.: P.E. attribute number x2 to start, plus 2D6 per level of experience."
  - name: "Psionics (Serpent Hunter)"
    description: "A Major Psychic with nine powers, I.S.P. costs as printed: Death Trance (2), Empathy (4), Impervious to Poison (4), Levitation (varies), Mind Block (4), Resist Fatigue (4), See the Invisible (4), Telekinetic Leap (8) and Telepathy (4). No other psionics are available. I.S.P.: 1D6x10 plus M.E. attribute number to start, +2D4 per level of experience."
  - name: "Conditional O.C.C. Bonuses"
    description: "+2 on Perception Rolls dealing with snakes, serpents, sea serpents, dragons and monsters. While riding a War Steed or sea serpent: +1 attack per melee and +1 to strike, parry and dodge. The save versus Horror Factor is +6 rather than +3 when fighting serpents, sea serpents, dragons and aquatic monsters."
restrictions:
  - "Alignment: any, but most are Principled or Scrupulous."
  - "Race: the page prints who takes up the Way of the Serpent Hunter as a breakdown - Lemurians 95%, Ichthyleans 2%, Merans 1%, humans and others 2%."
  - "SKILLS KNOWN BY ALL LEMURIANS are stored on this class at the figures its page prints: Language: Lemurian and Oceanic at 96%, Mathematics: Basic at 82% +1% per level, Swimming at 90% +1% per level. Language: Lemurian and Literacy: Lemurian are stored at the 98% of the O.C.C. Skills line Language and Literacy: Lemurian at 98%, above the 96% and the 85% +1% per level of the all-Lemurians lines."
  - "Horsemanship: none as a related skill, other than the O.C.C. skills. Electrical, Mechanical and Pilot Related: none."
  - "Pilot: Boat (sail or paddle type only), Jet Pack (Squid Packs) and Water Skiing & Surfing only."
  - "War Steeds: assigned a Thrall Serpent or Serpent Seahorse and one other serpent as his two personal War Steeds; can usually get access to any Lemurian War Steed depending on availability and the mission. These are creatures, not gear, and are not in the equipment list."
  - "Bio-Armor: Leviathan Bio-Armor is standard issue, but any other Bio-Armor may be preferred. Has access to all Bio-Skins."
  - "Money: a monthly salary of 2,300 credits or trade goods, double for squadron leaders; starts with one month''s pay. Often has an apartment or family home in a floating city; barracks house three Serpent Hunters."
  - "Cybernetics: none. Lemurians have no interest in bionics, not even Bio-Systems."
  - "Cannot learn new spells and has no psionics beyond the nine listed."
extraction_notes: |
  - Lemuria, printed 73-76 (printed 74 is a full-page illustration). Filed
    under the section heading "Lemurian Men-At-Arms O.C.C.s", so
    men_of_arms true and occ_group men-of-arms. No sdc_base or mdc_base is
    printed; the +4D6 S.D.C. is a pool bonus.
  - xp_table read off a render of printed 86, ladder headed "Serpent Hunter".
  - HAND TO HAND. The book prints "Hand to Hand: Martial Arts or Hand to
    Hand: Kapu Kuialua at the cost of one O.C.C. Related Skill". Stored as
    Martial Arts granted and demon_combat priced at one pick (Kapu Kuialua
    is held as Hand to Hand: Demon Combat). That is one reading of printed
    76; the line can also be read as either style costing one related skill.
  - HORSEMANSHIP: AQUATIC ANIMALS (+10%) OR EXOTIC ANIMALS. The +10% is
    printed on Aquatic Animals alone. Stored as a fixed grant of Aquatic
    Animals at 50 with the alternative in its note, because a choose group
    carries one bonus for every option and would put +10% on Exotic Animals.
  - LEMURIAN IS PRINTED TWICE: "Language and Literacy: Lemurian at 98%"
    under O.C.C. Skills and "Language: Lemurian and Oceanic at 96%" under
    Skills Known by All Lemurians. Lemurian stored at 98, Oceanic at 96.
  - LITERACY: LEMURIAN is printed at 98% (O.C.C. Skills, "Language and
    Literacy: Lemurian at 98%") and at 85% +1% per level (Skills Known by All
    Lemurians). Granted by name at 98, like the language, with the +1% per
    level of the all-Lemurians line, the only rate the page prints.
  - NO PER-LEVEL FIGURE IS PRINTED for Language: Lemurian or Language:
    Oceanic; 1 is stored for both, the native-speaker rate the skill
    descriptions print on printed 55.
  - P.P.E. The class is in group men-of-arms, so the Lemurian race does not
    yield its P.P.E. to it; overrides_race [ppe_base] makes the printed
    P.E. x2 +2D6 per level this class''s figure in a pairing.
  - SKILLS KNOWN BY ALL LEMURIANS are on the class, not left to the race,
    because the figures are this class''s own: Mathematics: Basic 82 and
    Swimming 90% +1% here against other figures on other O.C.C. pages.
  - AQUATIC SKILLS: ANY (+5%) has no catalog category. Stored as one
    related-skills entry named Aquatic whose only list names seven of the
    book''s Aquatic Skills (printed 54) at +5%. Left out: the eight this
    class grants as O.C.C. skills, and Ocean Geographic Surveying and
    Undersea Farming, which the page prints by name under Science at +5%.
  - Communication "Language, Literacy" are stored as Language: Other and
    Literacy: Other. Rogue''s Prowl is a Physical row and Communication''s
    Creative Writing and Language: Other are Technical rows; both real
    categories are granted. Physical is printed "+10% where applicable".
  - Conditional bonuses (perception, mounted attack and strike/parry/dodge,
    +6 vs Horror Factor, the slaying bonuses and critical strikes) are
    prose in special_abilities. Stored unconditionally: +1D4 M.E., P.S. and
    P.E., +4D6 S.D.C., +2 roll with impact, +3 vs Horror Factor.
  - Spell and psionic costs are printed beside each name on printed 75 and
    kept in the ability prose. The book''s "Impervious to Poison" is the
    held Impervious to Poison/Toxin. Levitation prints "(varies)".
  - Equipment: clothes are printed as uniforms, dress/formal wear and combat
    clothes and stored as three of clothing; "other common personal items"
    is not stored. The two choice lists are catalog sets, not printed lists.
  - The Pets and Familiars line on printed 75 says "Lemurian Guardsmen",
    carried over from the Oceanic Guardsman page; it also gives a designated
    War Steed of the player''s choice, which the equipment paragraph on
    printed 76 states more exactly.
