# Serpent Hunter

## Lore

Serpent Hunters are the Lemurian warriors who track, catch, tame and, when there is no other way, kill the sea serpents, dragons and monsters of the deep. To outsiders they are the best known of all Lemurians: mounted champions in the mould of a paladin, except that the mount is a giant serpent or one of the Gene-Mages'' engineered War Steeds rather than a horse.

Each Hunter keeps two steeds that belong to him alone. Rider and beast are trained to fight as one and to carry on fighting in concert after the rider has dismounted. When a Hunter dies his animals are marked so that nobody rides them again and are turned loose, and a Hunter who loses a steed grieves for weeks before he tames another.

Candidates are picked for fitness and skill at arms, and just as much for steadiness, honor and the ability to work in a team. The result is a warrior other troops will follow into the worst of a fight, who is nonetheless usually modest and plain-spoken. They are gentle with civilians and respectful of life, and entirely without mercy toward the minions of the Lord of the Deep, the Milu and the undead.

## GM Notes

Also called Serpent Riders and Serpent Bringers. A Hunter''s empathy does not extend to ordinary animals: with non-serpent animals he is at -20% on riding and other animal skills (printed 75). Squadron leaders draw double pay.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'serpent-hunter');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'serpent-hunter';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-serpent-hunter-class.sql');
